# Source: Fakhreddin Azimi, Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953,
# ch. 5, pp. 250–253. Mechanical effects are counterfactual abstractions.
title: <span class="term term-mossadegh">Mohammad Mossadegh</span>
new-page: true
is-pinned-card: true
tags: advisor

= {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mohammad Mossadegh{!</span>!}

[? if front_formed = 0 and attempt_emergency_seen = 0: {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}
remains outside any common opposition organization. His constitutional
authority is important, but the electoral protest that will bring opposition
figures together has not yet occurred. ?]
[? if front_formed = 0 and attempt_emergency_seen = 1: {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}
has been confined to his estates during the emergency. His constitutional
authority remains important, but the common electoral protest that will bring
the opposition together has not yet occurred. ?]
[? if front_formed = 1: {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}
is the central coordinating figure in the electoral protest that brought the
opposition coalition together. His intervention can help settle an immediate
question, but it cannot erase the coalition's differences. ?]

- @constitutional_case
- @hear_tendencies
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@constitutional_case
title: State the constitutional case
subtitle: <span class="term term-mossadegh">Mossadegh</span> gives unlike allies a constitutional formula they can repeat without sharing a full program
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if front_formed = 0: Available after the common electoral protest. ?][? if front_formed = 1: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; constitutional_legitimacy += 3; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 2; mossadegh_authority += 1

{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!} restates the coalition's demand for representative elections and
constitutional government, then tests each part of the argument against the
procedure the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}
expects the {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} to follow.

The coalition leaves with a case its different components can repeat without
claiming that {!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!} has resolved their wider disagreements.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@hear_tendencies
title: Hear the coalition's competing tendencies
subtitle: Each tendency is heard in its own language; agreement is postponed rather than forced
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if front_formed = 0: Available after the common electoral protest. ?][? if front_formed = 1: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; iran_party_relation += 1; toilers_relation += 1; independent_nationalists_relation += 1; religious_network_relation += 1; iran_party_dissent -= 1; toilers_dissent -= 1; independent_nationalists_dissent -= 1; religious_network_dissent -= 1

The discussion does not produce agreement, but it clarifies what the
cooperating circles expect from the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}.
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!} asks each tendency to
state the boundary it cannot cross and the narrower action it can support.

Participants are less likely to mistake consultation for an attempt to absorb
them, and working relations improve across the coalition.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing
